{"ticker":"BORORENEW","symbol":"BORORENEW","instrumentId":3028872,"name":"Borosil Renewables","industry":"NSE-Containers/Packaging","about":"Borosil Renewables Ltd. is a global leader in solar glass manufacturing, operating under the Borosil Group, which has a legacy of over six decades in glass production. With a state-of-the-art facility in Bharuch, Gujarat, the company boasts a production capacity of 1350 tons per day (TPD) following its acquisition of Europe’s Interfloat Group. Borosil Renewables is renowned for pioneering innovations like the world’s first fully tempered 2mm solar glass and antimony-free glass. Its products, compliant with international standards, cater to various solar applications, including utility-scale projects, BIPV, and specialized installations near airports, with ongoing expansions to reach 6 GW capacity by FY23.","website":"www.borosilrenewables.com","location":"Mumbai, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:10:11.803Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":380.2,"changePct":-1.1825860948667994,"week52High":651.65,"week52Low":370.3},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹5,596 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹1,633 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"64,760,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"106"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"11,956,192"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"0.49%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"3.53"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"0.7"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"6.0%"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.17"},{"label":"Beta","value":"1.58"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"0%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"12.57"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"21–528"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"8.5%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"30.18"},{"label":"Volume","value":"588,571"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"419,590"},{"label":"Master score","value":"55"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"66"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"10"},{"label":"Group rank"